import json,pathlib
root=pathlib.Path('.')
def read(p):return json.loads((root/p).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
def put(p,s):(root/p).write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
d=read('data/processed/environment_design.json');e=read('data/processed/environment_evaluation.json');g=read('data/processed/geographic_context.json');power=read('data/processed/power_daily.json');osm=read('data/processed/osm-water-source.json');elevation=read('data/processed/elevation_sources.json')
base=(root/'data/external/SOURCES.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8').split('<!-- environment -->')[0].split('\n## NASA POWER')[0].rstrip()
source=f'''\n\n<!-- environment -->
## Environmental addendum providers

- NASA POWER: [exact daily request]({power['provenance']['url']}), retrieved {power['provenance']['retrieved_at']}, SHA256 {power['provenance']['sha256']}. Variables PRECTOTCORR mm/day, T2M Celsius, RH2M percent. [Provider notes](POWER.md). [NASA citation](https://data.nasa.gov/dataset/prediction-of-worldwide-energy-resources-power). NASA government data; MERRA-2 / NASA GMAO. LST solar swath is not a civil timezone; cross-check only.
- OSM waterways/waterbodies: [exact Overpass query]({osm['url']}), retrieved {osm['retrieved_at']}, OSM timestamp {osm['osm_timestamp']}, SHA256 {osm['sha256']}. [Full query and source receipt](../processed/osm-water-source.json). Copyright OpenStreetMap contributors, [ODbL 1.0](https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). Primary overpass-api.de returned HTTP 406; the documented Private.coffee alternative returned a complete result. One bounded extract; no browser/provider traffic.
- Elevation: USGS SRTM90m via [Open Topo Data](https://www.opentopodata.org/datasets/srtm/); USGS public-domain data. Exactly {len(elevation)} batches, 2398 points on a 500m UTM grid. [Every exact request, timestamp, attribution and SHA256](../processed/elevation_sources.json). Cached raw srtm90m-grid-0.json through srtm90m-grid-2300.json plus provenance sidecars. API limit <=100 points/request; calls separated by >=1.3 seconds, <1000/day.
- Boundaries: [existing HDX/NAMRIA receipt](../geo/ncr-source.json), CC BY 3.0 IGO, geometry valid 2025-02-13. Areas derived from these official polygons, not represented as PSA land-area statistics. Fixed 2020 population remains unverified.
- Calendar seasons: [PAGASA climate definition](https://www.pagasa.dost.gov.ph/information/climate-philippines), verified 2026-10-25; June-November rainy, December-May dry; not an actual annual onset announcement.
- Biology: [CDC Aedes life cycle](https://www.cdc.gov/mosquitoes/about/life-cycle-of-aedes-mosquitoes.html/) and [container control](https://www.cdc.gov/mosquitoes/mosquito-control/mosquito-control-at-home.html), verified 2026-10-25. Container standing water is the primary biological context; mapped rivers are indirect proxies.
- Flood candidates checked: [UP NOAH Studio](https://noah.up.edu.ph/noah-studio), [UP DREAM products](https://dream.upd.edu.ph/products/index.html), [LiPAD access guide](https://lipad-fmc.dream.upd.edu.ph/help/) and [MGB maps](https://region11.mgb.gov.ph/geohazard-maps/). Portals/maps exist; no consistent NCR-wide, licensed analytical extract was retrieved/validated in this run. Omitted, without claiming such a dataset does not exist.
- Recent weather context: `npm run weather:refresh` caches raw weather-context-YYYY-MM-DD.json with exact-request receipt, exports public/api/v2/weather.json, and persists failed attempts too. One attempt per 24h on the server filesystem; no collection of viewer locations. Any available recent weather is context only; disease observations still end in 2023.
'''
put('data/external/SOURCES.md',base+source)
lines=['# Environment: sources, tests and honest limits','','This addendum replaces the weather/factors section of FINAL_REQUIREMENTS.md. The exact request is preserved in ENVIRONMENT_REQUIREMENTS.md. No raw disease files or hosted schema changed.','', '## Reproduce offline from caches','', 'Install Node 22 dependencies with `npm ci`, Python dependencies with `python -m pip install -r requirements-environment.txt`. Obtain source caches once with `npm run environment:fetch`. Then set `ENV_OFFLINE=1` and run `npm run evaluate` (PowerShell: `$env:ENV_OFFLINE="1"; npm run evaluate`). Evaluation performs no provider calls. It generates the original harness plus the separate environmental ablation, geographic effect sizes and figures. `npm run environment:prepare` reruns just the addendum.','', 'A clean clone needs the ignored public-provider caches. Transfer/download the exact URLs and matching receipts in data/external/SOURCES.md and data/processed/elevation_sources.json into data/external/. Required names: era5-manila-2015.json through era5-manila-2023.json; power-manila-2015-2023.json; osm-ncr-water.json; srtm90m-grid-0.json through srtm90m-grid-2300.json in steps of 100; each with .provenance.json. `environment:fetch` creates and validates receipts. Cache bytes are hashed; missing/bad data fails instead of being fabricated. No API keys are needed.','', '## Sources and weekly alignment','', 'See [exact requests, timestamps, licences and hashes](../data/external/SOURCES.md). ERA5 primary features use Asia/Manila civil dates, 24 hours/day, seven complete Monday-Sunday days/week. Rain days use a fixed >=1mm/day definition. Weekly rainfall is total mm; temperature mean/min/max Celsius; humidity mean percent. Incomplete weeks and invalid/fill values are rejected. The single Manila point does not measure station rainfall or resolve NCR cities. ERA5 grid about 25km; NASA POWER meteorology 0.5 by 0.625 degrees.','',f"NASA daily LST solar-swath cross-check: {d['comparison']['n']} paired weeks; rainfall Pearson r {d['comparison']['rainfall_r']:.6f}, temperature r {d['comparison']['temperature_r']:.6f}; rainfall MAE {d['comparison']['rainfall_mae_mm']:.3f} mm/week, temperature MAE {d['comparison']['temperature_mae_c']:.3f} Celsius. LST versus civil-day boundaries, different grids, downscaling and model bias limit agreement. This is not station validation, and POWER is not blended into features.", '', '## Frozen lags and small regularized models','',e['metadata']['training'],'',d['selection_rule'],'']
for scenario in ['Z','M']:
 l=d['lags'][scenario];lines.append(f"- {scenario}: rain lag {l['rain']}, temperature lag {l['temperature']}, humidity lag {l['humidity']}, rainfall rolling window {l['rain_window']} weeks; fixed cutoff {l['cutoff']}.")
lines+=['', 'All rainfall/temperature/humidity lags 1-8 and rainfall windows 1/2/4/8 are evaluated on training data only. The selected lag is frozen for all test horizons. Seasonal correlations are confounded; selection is a simple research heuristic, not optimal lag discovery. No multiple-testing correction or nested lag-tuning claim. Both scenarios have identical 2016-2017 training labels, hence identical lag choices.','', e['metadata']['features'],'', 'At most 15 inputs in the combined ridge (2 case lags, COVID, 3 calendar terms, 3 selected weather lags, 4 weather summaries, 2 onset terms). Covariates from a weather week ending after origin minus one week are never used. The cumulative-200mm proxy uses fully contained current-year weeks only; missing weeks invalidate it. Threshold 200mm and cap 26 weeks are fixed research definitions, not locally validated meteorological onset or PAGASA criteria. No test years select them.','', e['metadata']['thermal'],'', 'No optional ENSO, typhoon, satellite or school-calendar feature was added. No environmental feature is promoted to the public model because the primary evidence is inconclusive.','', '## Ablation findings','', 'Full numeric yearly/COVID/pooled MAE, RMSE, MASE, moving-block 95% skill CI, precision/recall/F1/AUC/Brier/FPR, interval coverage and episode lead: [ENVIRONMENT_RESULTS.md](ENVIRONMENT_RESULTS.md). Every model shares support within scenario and horizon, but this support differs from the original 8-lag harness. Do not compare their raw MAEs as an ablation.','', '|Scenario|1w persistence MAE|1w AR|1w season|1w weather|1w combined|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for scenario in ['Z','M']:
 def score(model,h=1):return next(s for s in e['summaries'] if s['scenario']==scenario and s['horizon']==h and s['model']==model and s['fold']=='test-2018-2023')
 lines.append('|'+scenario+'|'+ '|'.join(f"{score(m)['mae']:.3f}" for m in ['naive','env-ar','env-season','env-weather','env-season-weather'])+'|')
lines+=['', 'Season improves pooled one-week AR MAE by about 4.1% (Z) and 4.8% (M), yet remains worse than persistence. Unlike the supplied crude estimate, season worsens AR in 2022 and 2023 under this specification; it helps in 2018/2019. Some individual year/model point estimates beat persistence. No tested environmental variant establishes a positive lower 95% skill bound at 1 or 2 weeks in either scenario. This is inconclusive evidence, not proof of no effect.','', 'Exploratory four-week season and no-engineered combined variants have positive lower skill bounds in both scenarios in this run. Those gains do not justify a 1/2-week operational claim or promotion: exploratory horizon, multiple comparisons, selective M support and retrospective weather vintages remain limitations.','', 'The original all-lag weather regression finding remains valid on its separate cohort; the expanded controlled experiment is reported alongside it, not substituted silently.','', '## Monthly profile recheck','', '|Month of Sunday ending|Complete-row N|Mean cases/week|','|---:|---:|---:|']
for row in d['profile']:
 if row['scenario']=='M':lines.append(f"|{row['month']}|{row['complete_n']}|{row['complete_mean_cases']:.3f}|")
lines+=['', 'April/May means reproduce approximately 27/23 cases per week. August-October are about 95/122/93 in this complete-row specification, rather than the supplied 85-113 range. The weekly end-date assignment, source stitch, coverage and exclusion policy are explicit. A monthly profile does not measure a 2-3 month causal lag or establish the example 4-12 week warning claim; the app therefore uses calendar context and prevention guidance without asserting that delay. The descriptive profile includes test-period history but never selects model inputs.','', '## Geographic context (exploratory, n=17)','',g['metadata']['water'],'',g['metadata']['elevation'],'',g['metadata']['area'],'',g['metadata']['vintage'],'',g['metadata']['ci'],'',g['metadata']['confounding'],'','|Layer|Spearman rho|95% bootstrap CI|N|','|---|---:|---|---:|']
for row in g['correlations']:lines.append(f"|{row['feature']}|{row['rho']:.3f}|{row['low']:.3f} to {row['high']:.3f}|{row['n']}|")
lines+=['', 'All six geographic intervals cross zero. No geographic layer is claimed to forecast or cause dengue. Population density uses the unverified supplied 2020 denominator; the evidence remains provisional until PSA verification. Mean incidence is the mean of observed DOH weekly cases per fixed 100,000 population in 2016-2019, not zero-filled absent weeks or a current rate. There are 206 recorded source weeks per city.','',g['metadata']['biology'],'',g['metadata']['omitted'],'', 'No household risk map or optional barangay overlay was built. City context can be shown/hidden beside the historical comparison; no layer changes the forecast.','', '## Figures and descriptive drivers','', '- [Training-only lag correlations](figures/weather-lag-correlations.png)','- [Monthly profile](figures/monthly-case-profile.png)','- [Environment ablation by horizon](figures/environment-ablation.png)','- [Geographic scatterplots](figures/geographic-context.png)','', 'Standardized final-fit coefficients are descriptive only. Correlated weather variables, seasonal covariates and a small sample make attribution unstable; these coefficients do not select the deployed model.','', '|Scenario|Combined model feature|Standardized log-target coefficient|','|---|---|---:|']
for fit in e['drivers']:
 if fit['model']=='env-season-weather':
  for row in fit['rows']:lines.append(f"|{fit['scenario']}|{row['name']}|{row['value']:.5f}|")
lines+=['', '## Daily refresh and actual fallback','', '`npm run weather:refresh` is a server-side filesystem job. It persists a 24-hour attempt timestamp (including failures), locks concurrent refreshes, rate-limits requests and caches raw responses with receipts. A successful refresh of this revision returned a completed historical weather week; inspect public/api/v2/weather.json for its date. No browser calls a provider and no viewer coordinates are sent. No keys are exposed. This does not refresh disease observations or turn the app into live dengue surveillance.','', 'The public forecast is persistence in both availability states because environmental promotion was not justified. On failure, missing/stale weather status or absent weather features, the UI states "Weather data unavailable; showing baseline forecast." The same policy preserves the baseline forecast and its intervals. Rainy/dry calendar context remains available independently of weather. Tests simulate provider failure and the next attempt after 24 hours, as well as browser-level missing weather.','', 'Deployment scheduling was not applied. Run this job at most daily on one server with a persistent shared filesystem, then publish the static weather.json. Vercel immutable/serverless filesystems are not a durable shared cache: do not deploy this job as an unsynchronized request handler. For multiple workers, use a shared atomic cache/lock; no live hosted scheduler or weather API route is claimed.','', '## Remaining gates','', 'Original credential rotation, hosted Auth/migration/retention verification, deployed ZAP and DPO/human evaluation remain unresolved. New work does not enable reporting or alter official disease counts. No secrets, provider keys or raw community reports were added.']
put('docs/ENVIRONMENT.md','\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print('Updated ENVIRONMENT.md and provider source index from saved computed evidence.')
